{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","max_tokens":1024,"stream":true,"system":"You are a code assistant for a small Dart repository. Use the tools to read files; never guess file contents. Paths are relative to the repository root.","tools":[{"name":"read_file","description":"Read one text file of the repository at the pinned commit.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Repository-relative path, e.g. lib/a.dart"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"list_directory","description":"List the files under one directory of the repository.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Repository-relative directory, e.g. lib"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}}],"tool_choice":{"type":"auto"},"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","block_binding":{"prefix_mismatch_behavior":"error"}},"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How many seconds in total does the sync client wait across all of its retries? The policy is split across lib/a.dart, lib/b.dart and the file that lib/a.dart imports. First read lib/a.dart and lib/b.dart together (call read_file for both in the same step), then read the imported file, then work out the per-attempt delays carefully and give the total."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_51HOS3ClcJDZMg5sjxDzY3ll","name":"read_file","input":{"path":"lib/a.dart"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_37TLhnzFFooeColFBXbkG2Eb","name":"read_file","input":{"path":"lib/b.dart"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_51HOS3ClcJDZMg5sjxDzY3ll","content":"import 'c.dart';\n\n/// Retry policy for the sync client.\nconst retryBase = 3; // seconds\n"},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_37TLhnzFFooeColFBXbkG2Eb","content":"/// Number of retries after the first failure.\nconst retryCount = 5;\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_4414BSflTb7U5UFlIWk2OsPY","name":"read_file","input":{"path":"lib/c.dart"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_4414BSflTb7U5UFlIWk2OsPY","content":"/// Backoff shape used by lib/a.dart.\nconst multiplier = 2;\nconst maxDelay = 20; // seconds, cap applied to every attempt\n// delay(n) = min(retryBase * multiplier^n, maxDelay) for n = 0 .. retryCount - 1\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sync client waits **61 seconds** in total across its 5 retries.\n\nThe policy is spread over three files:\n- **lib/a.dart** sets `retryBase = 3` (seconds) and imports `c.dart`.\n- **lib/c.dart** (the imported file) sets `multiplier = 2` and `maxDelay = 20` (seconds). Its comment gives the formula `delay(n) = min(retryBase * multiplier^n, maxDelay)` for n = 0 to retryCount − 1.\n- **lib/b.dart** sets `retryCount = 5`.\n\nPer-attempt delays:\n\n| n | retryBase × 2^n | capped at 20 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 3 | 3 |\n| 1 | 6 | 6 |\n| 2 | 12 | 12 |\n| 3 | 24 | 20 |\n| 4 | 48 | 20 |\n\nTotal: 3 + 6 + 12 + 20 + 20 = **61 seconds**.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: lib/a.dart does not import lib/b.dart, so nothing in the code links `retryCount` to the delay formula. I used b.dart's value of 5 as you directed, and the formula's comment in c.dart is what ties the loop to that count."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"If retryCount were changed to 8 and maxDelay to 30, what would the total wait be? Work it out from what you already read; do not call tools."}]}]}